 30  Labour MPs could end up supporting this  sort of deal that you described do you  think that's roughly accurate I'm really  not sure but I think if a reasonable  deal is on the table the question I  think you know for some of my labour  colleagues is why wouldn't you support a  deal why would you why would you stand  along Boris Johnson or Jacob Riis MOG he  wants us to crash out without a deal and  that's the choice before it behind us so  if there was a vote of no-confidence in  Parliament in this government and you  would talk about universal credit  earlier on on the program I would be  there Jeremy Corbyn and other colleagues  voting for a photo of a girl confidence  against the government but this isn't  about a vote of confidence this is about  whether we crash out of the EU without a  deal and I really don't think that  serves the public's interest and I don't  think it serves Labour's interests to be  seen to be doing that but it's got to be  the right deal and that's why we've got  to make sure that we those of us who  want a deal you know actually push for  that and don't allow the no dealers to  take control okay Carolyn thank you very  much thank you
 

